<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Corrections</span><h1>How ToolboxKart handles corrections</h1><p>Software and search products change quickly. We review specific, evidence-backed correction requests and update material errors without hiding what changed.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container policy-copy"><div class="tool-content"><h2>Report an error</h2><p>Use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> and include the page URL, the statement you believe is wrong, a current supporting source and the date you checked it.</p><h2>What happens next</h2><p>We compare the report with current primary sources and the article's original evidence. A material factual error is corrected as soon as it can be verified. Minor grammar or formatting edits may be fixed without a separate notice.</p><h2>Dates and correction notes</h2><p>A substantive change receives an accurate modified date. When the correction changes a conclusion, price, limitation or important recommendation, the page should explain the change clearly. Dates are not refreshed merely for search visibility.</p><h2>Company requests</h2><p>Vendors may submit updated facts, but they do not control the article. We do not remove a supported limitation or negative fit assessment simply because a company disagrees with it.</p></div></div></section><?php require __DIR__.'/includes/footer.php';?>
